WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:03.300
-We are now just
over a week away

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:05.434
from the most consequential
midterm elections

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:07.300
in recent memory
and Republicans have made

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:08.501
their priorities very clear --

00:00:08.501 --> 00:00:10.234
continue spreading
conspiracy theories

00:00:10.234 --> 00:00:11.868
about the 2020 election,

00:00:11.868 --> 00:00:14.501
intimidate people trying to vote
in this election,

00:00:14.501 --> 00:00:16.734
and claim preemptively
that the results

00:00:16.734 --> 00:00:18.667
must be illegitimate,
if they lose.

00:00:18.667 --> 00:00:21.133
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:21.133 --> 00:00:25.334
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:25.334 --> 00:00:27.801
These are anxiety-ridden times,

00:00:27.801 --> 00:00:29.100
so, let's start
with the good news.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.501
Thanks to new,
relaxed COVID restrictions

00:00:31.501 --> 00:00:33.567
in the building,
our cue card guy, Wally,

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:36.701
no longer has to wear
a face shield during the show.

00:00:36.701 --> 00:00:38.033
Now, that's true
of everyone here,

00:00:38.033 --> 00:00:40.300
but Wally's face shield
was different.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:41.901
Want to tell them why, Wally?

00:00:41.901 --> 00:00:44.067
-Yeah, mine had a tiny,
wet sponge on it.

00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:46.801
-Wally's had a tiny,
wet sponge on it.

00:00:46.801 --> 00:00:49.701
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.701 --> 00:00:52.767
Wally, you want to tell them
why it had a tiny, wet sponge?

00:00:52.767 --> 00:00:55.067
-Yeah, well, I couldn't lick my
fingers between each cue card,

00:00:55.067 --> 00:00:57.033
so, I needed the sponge
for moisture.

00:00:57.033 --> 00:00:58.534
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.534 --> 00:01:01.601
-He couldn't use his tongue...

00:01:01.601 --> 00:01:03.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.601
...so, he had a tiny,
wet sponge.

00:01:06.601 --> 00:01:07.901
He couldn't do this --

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:10.367
...so we had to do this --

00:01:10.367 --> 00:01:12.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.734 --> 00:01:15.334
And, for over two years,
I've had to read cue cards

00:01:15.334 --> 00:01:16.734
while looking at that,
thinking to myself,

00:01:16.734 --> 00:01:19.334
"That sponge is a stand-in
for a human tongue,"

00:01:19.334 --> 00:01:21.334
[ Laughter ]
and I dare anyone here,

00:01:21.334 --> 00:01:23.367
I dare any person here
or watching

00:01:23.367 --> 00:01:25.434
to see a mask today that's more
disgusting than that.

00:01:25.434 --> 00:01:27.100
Happy [Bleep] Halloween,
everybody.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:28.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:28.734 --> 00:01:31.367
[ Cheering ]

00:01:31.367 --> 00:01:33.701
My national nightmare is over.

00:01:33.701 --> 00:01:35.033
[ Laughter ]
Moving on.

00:01:36.267 --> 00:01:37.667
Wally, I said, moving on.

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:39.133
Ugh!

00:01:39.133 --> 00:01:40.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:43.834
[ Applause ]

00:01:46.601 --> 00:01:49.734
Republicans have made it clear,
if they win back power,

00:01:49.734 --> 00:01:51.434
they'll do things
like impeach Joe Biden,

00:01:51.434 --> 00:01:52.868
pass a national abortion ban,

00:01:52.868 --> 00:01:54.300
and threaten to detonate
the economy

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.534
to force cuts to Social Security
and Medicare.

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:57.868
But it's not just Congress

00:01:57.868 --> 00:01:59.267
where pivotal elections
are being held.

00:01:59.267 --> 00:02:02.467
Pro-Trump Republican election
deniers across the country

00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:04.901
are running for key positions
that would allow them

00:02:04.901 --> 00:02:06.834
to supervise elections
in swing states

00:02:06.834 --> 00:02:08.167
and some are poised to win.

00:02:08.167 --> 00:02:11.000
The Washington Post conducted
an exhaustive survey

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.200
and found that a majority
of GOP nominees

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:16.801
on the ballot this fall deny
or question the 2020 results,

00:02:16.801 --> 00:02:18.267
and the website
FiveThirtyEight found

00:02:18.267 --> 00:02:20.434
that most of those candidates
are likely to win.

00:02:20.434 --> 00:02:22.033
-60% of Americans
are going to have

00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:24.534
an election denier
on the ballot this fall.

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:28.000
Of the 552 Republican nominees
running for office,

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:31.501
200 have fully denied the
legitimacy of the 2020 election.

00:02:31.501 --> 00:02:34.234
-We simply cannot have
a functioning democracy

00:02:34.234 --> 00:02:35.801
where one party denies
the legitimacy

00:02:35.801 --> 00:02:36.801
of any election they don't win.

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:37.968
You don't see Jets fans

00:02:37.968 --> 00:02:39.200
spraying champagne
on each other,

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:40.767
claiming they beat
the Patriots yesterday,

00:02:40.767 --> 00:02:42.501
[ Laughter ]
even though they lost 22-17.

00:02:42.501 --> 00:02:44.534
Yeah, the Jets jokes
are back, baby!

00:02:44.534 --> 00:02:45.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:45.534 --> 00:02:46.601
After a red --

00:02:46.601 --> 00:02:48.901
After a red-hot start
to the season,

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:50.701
the Jets lost to their bitter
division rivals

00:02:50.701 --> 00:02:52.968
at home yesterday, so, this
morning, first thing I did,

00:02:52.968 --> 00:02:54.367
I walked right
up to our security guard,

00:02:54.367 --> 00:02:57.033
Jim Brier, and I said, "How
about those jets yesterday?"

00:02:57.033 --> 00:02:59.501
And he said, "Stand back,
or I'll crush your head

00:02:59.501 --> 00:03:01.300
like a peanut, joke man."

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.434
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:03.434 --> 00:03:05.734
And then I said, "Yes, sir,"
because I respect Jim,

00:03:05.734 --> 00:03:09.200
because at no point did he wear
a tiny, wet sponge on his face.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:10.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.868 --> 00:03:12.534
Take, for example,
the GOP's nominee

00:03:12.534 --> 00:03:14.000
for secretary of state
in Arizona,

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.300
a guy named Mark Finchem.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:19.200
Finchem was actually
at the Capitol on January 6th

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:21.767
and has been interviewed
by the January 6th Committee.

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:23.934
In fact, just a few weeks ago,
Finchem, who is currently

00:03:23.934 --> 00:03:26.434
leading many polls
for secretary of state,

00:03:26.434 --> 00:03:28.267
which supervises
Arizona's elections, tweeted...

00:03:32.534 --> 00:03:34.133
...which is the worst

00:03:34.133 --> 00:03:35.767
Mariah Carey cover
I've ever heard.

00:03:35.767 --> 00:03:37.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.467
And, of course, it will not
shock you to learn

00:03:38.467 --> 00:03:39.734
that these lunatics
have absolutely

00:03:39.734 --> 00:03:41.334
no evidence, whatsoever,
for their lies.

00:03:41.334 --> 00:03:43.434
In fact, Finchem
was asked directly

00:03:43.434 --> 00:03:46.734
by a reporter for Time magazine
if he would certify Biden

00:03:46.734 --> 00:03:48.367
as the winner
of the 2024 election,

00:03:48.367 --> 00:03:49.801
if Biden gets the most votes,

00:03:49.801 --> 00:03:51.567
and this is how
the exchange went.

00:03:51.567 --> 00:03:52.667
Finchem told the reporter...

00:04:07.367 --> 00:04:10.667
Well, where were you looking,
in the crowd on January 6th?

00:04:10.667 --> 00:04:12.367
[ Laughter ]
Do you think maybe,

00:04:12.367 --> 00:04:13.601
if someone voted for Joe Biden,

00:04:13.601 --> 00:04:15.067
they wouldn't want to say
that to you,

00:04:15.067 --> 00:04:18.400
a [bleep] looney tune who asks
Santa for Christmas arrests?

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:20.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:21.334
Other than that, solid logic.

00:04:21.334 --> 00:04:22.634
That's his argument --
if you don't personally

00:04:22.634 --> 00:04:24.033
know anyone who voted
for Joe Biden,

00:04:24.033 --> 00:04:26.334
then, by logical extension,
no one voted for Joe Biden.

00:04:26.334 --> 00:04:27.767
In fact,
now that you mention it,

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:29.200
if you never met Joe Biden

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:30.901
and you don't know anyone
who's met Joe Biden,

00:04:30.901 --> 00:04:32.501
then how do you even know
Joe Biden exists?

00:04:32.501 --> 00:04:34.567
[ Laughter ]
He's probably not even real.

00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:36.367
That's why he gets stuck
on stage sometimes

00:04:36.367 --> 00:04:37.467
and freezes in place.

00:04:37.467 --> 00:04:39.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:39.601 --> 00:04:42.133
He's actually just
a computer simulation

00:04:42.133 --> 00:04:44.834
and what we're seeing
is a glitch.

00:04:44.834 --> 00:04:46.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:48.167
By the way, if you recently
bought a tech company,

00:04:48.167 --> 00:04:49.601
that whole glitch thing
was a joke,

00:04:49.601 --> 00:04:51.734
not something for you to post
and say, "Food for thought."

00:04:51.734 --> 00:04:53.834
[ Laughter ]
And, sure enough,

00:04:53.834 --> 00:04:55.434
all these stolen election lies

00:04:55.434 --> 00:04:57.000
are having very real
consequences.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:59.901
In Arizona, for example,
